## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a compliant, scalable multi-tenant ML workflow on GCP with governance, explainability, and safety nets.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-aware Vertex AI deployment (endpoints/regions)
- Per-tenant Feature Stores and Model Registry
- Data residency and lineage via Data Catalog
- Explainable AI and per-tenant fairness checks
- Drift detection and safe rollback via canaries
- Monitoring/alerts with Cloud Monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo drift monitor for a tenant
function monitorDrift(tenant, current, baseline){
  const p = ksTest(current, baseline);
  if(p < 0.05){
    triggerRollback(tenant);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant drift detectors in staging?
- How do you ensure no data leakage across tenants while sharing infra?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes how a candidate designs a privacy-conscious, multi-tenant ML pipeline on GCP, balancing data governance, per-tenant isolation, cost, and operability.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation with per-tenant datasets and Feature Store
- PII de-identification in Dataflow
- Canary deployments and traffic shifting
- Drift detection and Explainable AI for governance
- Privacy logging and rollback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: shift partial traffic to canary on drift alert
function rollbackOnDrift(isDrift, canaryEndpoint, prodEndpoint){
  if(!isDrift) return;
  // gradually shift traffic back to prod
  setTraffic(canaryEndpoint, 0.0);
  setTraffic(prodEndpoint, 1.0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding with data retention?
- How would you scale feature store lookups for thousands of tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving ML at scale with regulatory constraints, multi-tenant isolation, and production-grade governance. Requires knowledge of Vertex AI Confidential Computing, Dataflow pipelines, Data Catalog/DLP, and automated rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI Confidential Computing (VMs/TPUs)
- Dataflow ingestion and residency controls
- Private endpoints and per-tenant budgets
- Data Catalog governance and DLP coverage
- Adversarial robustness testing and dataset/versioning

## Code Example
